{"title":"Edit Distance (Delete/Replace Only)","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given two strings `S1` and `S2`. You may apply two kinds of operations to `S1`, each costing one operation:\n\n- **delete** any single character of the current string;\n- **replace** any single character of the current string with any other lowercase letter.\n\nThere is no insert operation. Find the minimum number of operations needed to convert `S1` into `S2` (for example `comb` into `cat` takes 3 operations: delete one letter and replace two). If it is impossible, print `-1`.\n\nSince characters can only be deleted or replaced, the string never grows, so the conversion is impossible exactly when `S2` is longer than `S1`.","inputFormat":"The first line contains the string `S1`.\nThe second line contains the string `S2`.","outputFormat":"Print a single integer: the minimum number of delete and replace operations, or `-1` if `S1` cannot be converted into `S2`.","constraints":["1 ≤ |S1|, |S2| ≤ 1000","Both strings consist of lowercase letters a-z"],"examples":[{"input":"comb\ncat","output":"3","explanation":"Delete one character of `comb` (say `b`) to get `com`, then replace `o` with `a` and `m` with `t`. No way of choosing which letter to delete leaves fewer than two mismatches against `cat`."},{"input":"abcde\nbd","output":"3","explanation":"Delete `a`, `c` and `e`; the remaining `bd` already equals `S2`."},{"input":"ab\nabc","output":"-1","explanation":"`S2` is longer than `S1` and there is no insert operation."}],"tests":[{"input":"a\na","output":"0"},{"input":"a\nb","output":"1"},{"input":"a\nab","output":"-1"},{"input":"abc\nabc","output":"0"},{"input":"xyz\nabc","output":"3"},{"input":"aaaa\na","output":"3"},{"input":"abab\nba","output":"2"},{"input":"babaaaba\naabaaa","output":"3"},{"input":"aab\nb","output":"2"},{"input":"babaaaa\nbabba","output":"3"},{"input":"ecbld\ngvcmwgarxm","output":"-1"},{"input":"cacabbacc\nabbbbbbba","output":"7"},{"input":"aaab\na","output":"3"